-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party parts

1. Distance formulas by Inigo Quilez (src/sdf.js, src/parts.js, src/cave.js):
   the polynomial smooth minimum (smin / smax), the bound-corrected ellipsoid
   distance and the exact round cone (sdRoundCone), from his articles
   "Distance functions" and "Smooth minimum" at https://iquilezles.org.
   Those snippets are published under the MIT License,
   Copyright (c) Inigo Quilez, with the same terms as the licence above.
   Keep this notice with any copy of these formulas.

2. Simplex noise (src/noise.js) follows Stefan Gustavson's public-domain
   reference implementation ("Simplex noise demystified", 2005). Public domain.

3. mulberry32 random number generator (src/noise.js) by Tommy Ettinger.
   Public domain.

4. hash2 (src/noise.js) and the value-noise hash (src/sdf.js) use the 32-bit
   prime constants of xxHash by Yann Collet (BSD 2-Clause); only the constants
   are used, no xxHash code.

5. Surface nets is a public algorithm (S. Gibson, "Constrained elastic surface
   nets", 1998); this implementation was written for the games.

three.js (installed by npm, used by src/geometry.js, src/streamer.js and the
demo): MIT License, Copyright (c) 2010-2026 three.js authors.
